   "answer": "Under Regulation E, the standard investigation period is 45 days after the bank receives a notice of error. The bank may extend that period to **90 days** (instead of 45 days) when the notice of error involves an electronic fund transfer that meets any of the following conditions:\n\n1. The transfer **was not initiated within a state** (i.e., it was an out‑of‑state transaction);  \n2. The transfer **resulted from a point‑of‑sale debit‑card transaction**; or  \n3. The transfer **occurred within 30 days after the first deposit to the account was made**.  \n\nIn those situations, the bank is allowed up to 90 days to complete its investigation and determine whether an error occurred【1005.11(c)#3】.",
